## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) >= 18
- [pnpm](https://pnpm.io/) (installed automatically via [corepack](https://nodejs.org/api/corepack.html))
<% if (database === 'postgresql' && docker) { %>- [Docker](https://www.docker.com/) (for the generated PostgreSQL and full-stack Compose workflows)<% } else if (database === 'postgresql') { %>- A reachable PostgreSQL server<% } %>

> **Don't have pnpm?** Node.js includes corepack. Run `corepack enable` once, then `pnpm install` will automatically download the correct pnpm version.

### Install Dependencies

```bash
pnpm install
```

`postinstall` generates the Prisma client. Root `predev` and `prebuild` run it again as a safety net when install scripts were skipped.

### Environment Variables

API env lives in `apps/api/.env` (see `apps/api/.env.example`).

<% if (includeWeb) { %>Web env: `apps/web/.env.local` (see `.env.local.example`).

<% } %><% if (database === 'postgresql' && docker) { %>
### Option 1: Run the Full Stack with Docker

```bash
docker compose up --build -d
```

Compose waits for PostgreSQL, applies existing migrations, and starts the API<%= includeWeb ? ', web app,' : '' %> and Prisma Studio.

### Option 2: Run the Apps Locally

1. Start PostgreSQL:

```bash
docker compose up -d postgres
```

> **PostgreSQL port:** Docker maps Postgres to **localhost:5433** (`apps/api/.env` `DATABASE_URL`).

2. Generate the Prisma client and apply migrations from the project root:

```bash
pnpm run db:setup
```

3. Start dev servers from the **project root** (builds and watches `packages/contracts`):

```bash
pnpm dev
```
<% } else if (database === 'postgresql') { %>
### Run Locally

1. Start PostgreSQL and verify `DATABASE_URL` in `apps/api/.env` points to it.

2. Generate the Prisma client and apply migrations:

```bash
pnpm run db:setup
```

3. Start dev servers from the **project root**:

```bash
pnpm dev
```
<% } else { %>
### Run Locally

```bash
pnpm run db:setup
pnpm dev
```

Run `pnpm dev` from the project root so `packages/contracts` is built and watched.
<% } %>

